# Repo roles

Two checkouts share this product. Put the change in the repo that owns that kind of work.

| Work | Repo | Path | Branch |
|------|------|------|--------|
| Servers, Docker, containers, identity, annotation, export, OData, segmentation, section correction, `gRPC_Protos`, and the gRPC clients (the gRPC Viking, Jotunn) | **Viking** | `d:\src\git\Viking` | `dev` |
| WCF clients (Viking, VikingAU, MonogameTestbed, shared client libraries) and the production WCF annotation server (`Servers/AnnotationService`, built and deployed from here); Viking Test builds are packed from here | **Viking-Net4.8** | `d:\src\git\Viking-Net4.8` | `Net4.8` |

This repo's `Net4.8` branch was called `Legacy` until 2026-11-01, and the checkout was `D:\src\git\VikingLegacy`; older commits, plans and reports use those names.

## Keep clients in parallel

Viking has a `Clients/` tree too: the gRPC client was ported from Viking-Net4.8's. Keep the two aligned so fixes reach both.

- Land WCF client changes in **Viking-Net4.8** first.
- Mirror the same change into Viking `Clients/` (and any shared client projects it touches) on a best-effort basis in the same piece of work, where the gRPC client has the same code.
- If a client fix is made in Viking and it affects the WCF client, back port it into Viking-Net4.8 the same way.
- Do not let the two client trees drift when the mirror is practical in the same change.

Server and container changes stay in Viking; the one exception is the WCF annotation server, which lives only in Viking-Net4.8.

```text
WCF Viking annotation fix
  → edit Clients/Viking in Viking-Net4.8
  → mirror the same edit under Clients/ in Viking

IdentityServer compose / cert change
  → edit Servers/ in Viking only
```
